# Maps this repo's commit history to a public-safe identity for display
# (GitHub, `git log --use-mailmap`, `git shortlog`) — it does NOT rewrite any
# commit, so hashes and the raw author record are untouched. See
# docs/yol-2026-09-23.md Aşama 12 for why: the real address below was used
# for every commit before publish; this repo was never force-pushed/rewritten
# to remove it, so the mailmap is the only public-facing fix.
#
# id+ without the numeric GitHub user id still routes correctly on GitHub in
# practice; replace with the real numeric id (Settings > Emails) if you want
# the exact canonical form.
